{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"926","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"G. Large Bouquets"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A flower shop has got "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" bouquets, and the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th bouquet consists of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":" flowers. Vasya, the manager of the shop, decided to make large bouquets from these bouquets. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Vasya thinks that a bouquet is large if it is made of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"two or more"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" initial bouquets, and there is a constraint: the total number of flowers in a large bouquet should be "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"odd"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". Each of the initial bouquets can be a part of at most one large bouquet. If an initial bouquet becomes a part of a large bouquet, all its flowers are included in the large bouquet."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Determine the maximum possible number of large bouquets Vasya can make. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single positive integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n ≤ 105"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of initial bouquets."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains a sequence of integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a1, a2, ..., an"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ ai ≤ 106"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of flowers in each of the initial bouquets."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print the maximum number of large bouquets Vasya can make. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5\n2 3 4 2 7\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"6\n2 2 6 8 6 12\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n11 4 10\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example Vasya can make "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":" large bouquets. For example, the first bouquet can contain the first and the fifth initial bouquets (the total number of flowers is then equal to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"9"},{"kind":"text","text":"), and the second bouquet can consist of the second and the third initial bouquets (the total number of flowers is then equal to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"7"},{"kind":"text","text":"). The fourth initial bouquet is unused in this scheme. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example it is not possible to form a single bouquet with odd number of flowers."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third example Vasya can make one large bouquet. For example, he can make it using all three initial bouquets. The size of the large bouquet is then equal to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"11 + 4 + 10 = 25"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"G","problemCode":"926G","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/926/problem/G"}